{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520941-v20-various-doubts","id":1520941,"title":"V20 Various Doubts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-19T07:14:21-07:00","id":1520941,"title":"V20 Various Doubts","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> I have multiple unrelated questions for V20, can you help me find the answers?<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Can you have both <b>Disfigured </b>and <b>Monstrous </b>flaws?<br /> <i>The latter has a lower limit on Appearance but the former imposes a Social penalty so I think both have an actual effect without too much overlap.</i></li> <li>For the purpose of<b> Methuselah\u2019s Thirst</b> flaw, what count as mortals? Can you feed on ghouls?\u200b<br /> <i>The flaw states you can only feed on Kindred or other supernatural creatures, so are ghouls supernatural enough to count?</i></li> <li>How do Tremere share rituals? If you develop a ritual, how gets disseminated to the world?<br /> <i>Relevant to the &quot;Ward versus Cathayans&quot; ritual (San Francisco by Night) whose write up mentions that everyone that knows it is in Las Vegas Chantry... How long and what way will this ritual get shared to say, Vienna, Japan, etc.</i></li> <li>Did Augustus Giovanni swear any kind of fealty or loyalty oath, any kind of official promise to Cappadocious? Or was the expected loyalty to a sire what got broken there?<br /> <i>I am thinking on socially how the betrayal was taken, and what were the shock factors: an Ante got eaten but what about Augustus reputation as someone &quot;trustworthy&quot; to deal with, if he ate his maker, why would I deal with him.</i></li> <li>Are the Kindred of the East books compatible with V20? What changes (if any) are needed to use them with V20?<br /> <i>I am thinking only of the Dodge ability, the experience costs that are exaggerated for the Kuei-Jin and removing the non standard abilities (but the hobby talent/skill/knowledge could also put them to use).</i></li> <li>Are the Mummy books compatible with V20? What changes (if any) are needed to use them with V20?</li> <li>What do you roll in a crossover game when a discipline usage asks for some stat you lack?<br /> <i>For example neither a W20 werewolf nor a M20 mage have Humanity or Virtues, what do you roll when a Discipline ask for those values?</i></li> <li>Which discipline better represents old civilization magic: <b>Thaumaturgy</b>, <b>Koldunic Sorcery</b>, or an assortment of Disciplines?<br /> <i>Essentially, what would old Egypt/Mesopotamia vampires have, I understand that Thaumaturgy is a recent invention, and that Koldunic Sorcery is Tzimisce but which one repressents the primal magic (Same way that Cruac does for Requiem).</i>\u200b</li> </ol>Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":".  Added a question. 08-20-2023, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T18:53:19-07:00","id":1521000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520941-v20-various-doubts#post1520941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the purpose of<b> Methuselah\u2019s Thirst</b> flaw, what count as mortals? Can you feed on ghouls?\u200b\u200bThe flaw states you can only feed on Kindred or other supernatural creatures, so are ghouls supernatural enough to count?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say no. It is ridiculously east for vampires to create ghouls, so allowing that would easily subvert what that does. However, since ghouls do have vitae in them in the form of actual Blood Points, I would allow the Methusaleh (or whoever had that flaw) to gain those Blood Points (and only those blood points which is usually only 1) as long as they drained the ghoul of their entire blood pool, killing them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520941-v20-various-doubts#post1520941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]How do Tremere share rituals? If you develop a ritual, how gets disseminated to the world?<br /> Relevant to the &quot;Ward versus Cathayans&quot; ritual (San Francisco by Night) whose write up mentions that everyone that knows it is in Las Vegas Chantry... How long and what way will this ritual get shared to say, Vienna, Japan, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say it is the normal learning rituals (page 230). Other than time required, there does not need to be any rolls. Though if a gaming group wanted there to be some mechanic to do so, I'd probably pick an Intelligence + Occult roll with the number of successes needed equal to the level of the rite, with each roll coming after a set amount of time appropriate for each rite level (day for level 1, week for level 2, month for level 3, season for level 4, year for level 5). It's all about what works for the game group.<br /> <br /> In terms of how quickly a rite can spread, it all depends on how you view the setting and Clan Tremere. There is no one correct way. But here is what I do. I typically divide rites into &quot;common&quot;, &quot;uncommon&quot;, &quot;rare&quot; and &quot;proprietary&quot; rites. Common rites well known to most Tremere, and these can be learned at their chantry as long as a Tremere is in good standing. Regents are expected to teach these rites to Apprentices provided they follow the Pyramid. Uncommon rites are not so well known, but not exactly secret knowledge. These can get taught, but usually only as favors and gaining of boons. Rare rites are closely guarded secrets to the individual vampires who have them. They only teach them to trusted companions, minions, etc. and always require something in exchange (boons, other closely guarded knowledge and secrets, partial blood bonds, etc.). Proprietary rites are even more closely guarded secrets that belong to specific factions within the Pyramid, and they never get taught to those who are not of that faction. That might be members of a particularly isolated Chantry with fanatical loyalty to their Regent, one of the secret conspiracies within the Tremere, or whatever else you can imagine.<br /> <br /> As for Ward versus Cathayans? It depends on how much of a threat the Catahyans represent to the Tremere. In most chronicles, I'd likely make it a Rare rite. Its inventor wants favors from others to teach it to them. But if you go Revised metaplot and have the Cathayans conduct nonsensical mass attacks everywhere, its importance would grow and would quickly transition to an uncommon or even common rite for simple survival. Probably with rapid promotion of its inventor in the Pyramid hierarchy as thanks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520941-v20-various-doubts#post1520941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Did Augustus Giovanni swear any kind of fealty or loyalty oath, any kind of official promise to Cappadocious? Or was the expected loyalty to a sire what got broken there?<br /> I am thinking on socially how the betrayal was taken, and what were the shock factors: an Ante got eaten but what about Augustus reputation as someone &quot;trustworthy&quot; to deal with, if he ate his maker, why would I deal with him.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Giovanni are supposed to be seen as disgusting Devil Kindred and absolutely abhorred by other Kindred, and the only reason they were not wiped out was because of the Promise of 1528. So their reputation among other vampires is supposed to be low. However, this often gets lost and Giovanni vampires treated like they were just anyone else as opposed to a fringe group that is detested by all others. So in my chronicles, I portray them as being heavily discriminated against and disliked with extreme prejudice. However, I generally do not see this when playing in another ST's games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T00:01:31-07:00","id":1521011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520941-v20-various-doubts#post1520941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,<br /> <br /> I have multiple unrelated questions for V20, can you help me find the answers?<br /> <br /> Can you have both <b>Disfigured </b>and <b>Monstrous </b>flaws?<br /> <i>The latter has a lower limit on Appearance but the former imposes a Social penalty so I think both have an actual effect without too much overlap.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520941-v20-various-doubts#post1520941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,<br /> <br /> <br /> For the purpose of<b> Methuselah\u2019s Thirst</b> flaw, what count as mortals? Can you feed on ghouls?\u200b<br /> The flaw states you can only feed on Kindred or other supernatural creatures, so are ghouls supernatural enough to count?</div> </div> </div> </div>No... and yes<br /> Ghouls have Human blood, some of it replaced by Vitae<br /> As Black Fox said, the Vampire in question can drink the vitae out, but the rest is useless for him, and if it wasn't Her ghoul? Blood bond forms... so dangerous snack.<br /> Ravenants are a bit complicated, since their bodies naturally produce a weak vampire-like vitae, which sustains their bodies far beyond normal human lifespans (although not immortal, revenants can live to be hundreds of years old; they age at approximately one-quarter the rate humans do), and also gives them the ability to use Disciplines.<br /> They are hibris, between mortal and vampire, so Storyteller's descretion<br /> Personally I would say yes<br /> On the similar note, I would say Typhon's Brew (Most preparation of Setite alchemy begin with this magical, vitae-laced beer. A lector-priest who does not know how to create Typhon's Brew can forget about pursuing further knowledge of alchemy. This beer sustains ghouls as if it were true vampiric vitae. Vampires can drink it too. By itself, Typhon's Brow has no other properties. It cannot be used to Embrace a mortal, nor to blood bond the imbiber: The brewing process negates this aspect of the vitae.<br /> <b>System:</b> Brewing the Typhon's brew takes a full month, beginning and ending at the dark of the moon. For every gallon brewed, the alchemist includes one blood point's worth of his own vitae. The brewing process multiplies the vitae, so that a ghoul can gain one blood point per quart of the magic beer. Vampires, however, gain only one blood point per gallon consumed - the same rate as in brewing the beer. For vampires, the beer's magic is limited to the fact that they can drink it at all without heaving it up seconds later. They can even get drunk on it, and suffer a hangover later.) made by Akhu would also work<br /> Similarly, the Blood-Horn of Odin (The Blood-Horn was among the treasured artifacts of the All-High who ruled much of Scandinavia during the period of the Vikings. When one drop of blood was added to the ale within, the whole liquid would change into blood. The same would occur with vampiric vitae and mead, which made it possible for the All-High and his einherjar to substain themselves without leaving his temple in Uppsala.) or similar Artifact could also work<br /> Not to mention there is a bit forgotten secondary skill from &quot;Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand&quot;.on page 70, named &quot;Blood Preparation&quot;:<br /> <br /> <b>Blood Preparation</b><br /> You know the effects of various substances on the blood. You can use this knowledge to recognize foreign substances in any blood you taste, and you also know the art of feeding your victims certain substances to get the desired taste and effects. You are knowledgeable in chemicals, intoxicants, herbs, spices and food and how they affect mortal and inmortal blood. You can prepare a variety of flavours for blood feasts, and are capable of combining this art with Toxicology to make the blood of a living mortals dangerous to the Kindred.<br /> * Novice: You are a dabller; you can prepare simple meals.<br /> ** Practiced: Yot know several recipes and can perpare a variety of meals.<br /> *** Competent: You know many recipes, though you have trouble preparing truly exotic cusine.<br /> **** Expert: You are and excellent chef; you know all the great recipes as well as a wide range of exotic recipes.<br /> ***** Master: You are a master chef; you know a great variety of recipes and you can create your own masterpieces.<br /> Possesed by: Some Toreador, Sabbat, baba Yaga's chefs, Black Hand Kindred and some cannibals.<br /> Specialities: Intoxicants, Spices, Easy-to-prepare meals, Kindred Poisons, Recognizing and Analysing Tastes.<br /> Blood foods, blood-bread, blood-puding, blood-wine, several blood sweets... a nice feast is always fun in an Elysium or in an Elder's banquet hall especially if your host is on the Via Voluptarius/Path of Pleasure <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Vampire parties can be fun\u200b<br /> And we not even mentioned Kiasyd mixology...<br /> But i digress<br /> <br /> So, ghouls, yes and and no<br /> Ravenant, yes - in my personal opinion<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520941-v20-various-doubts#post1520941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are the Kindred of the East books compatible with V20? What changes (if any) are needed to use them with V20?<br /> I am thinking only of the Dodge ability, the experience costs that are exaggerated for the Kuei-Jin and removing the non standard abilities (but the hobby talent/skill/knowledge could also put them to use).</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say yes<br /> But I think the Storyteller's vault have a KotE guide for that<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520941-v20-various-doubts#post1520941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the Mummy books compatible with V20? What changes (if any) are needed to use them with V20?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Mummy: The Resurrection is a bit of a &quot;replacement&quot; of the original Mummy books<br /> Actually the two mummies are two seperate &quot;breed&quot;<br /> But both are technically compatible with any 20th edition material<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520941-v20-various-doubts#post1520941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you roll in a crossover game when a discipline usage asks for some stat you lack?<br /> For example neither a W20 werewolf nor a M20 mage have Humanity or Virtues, what do you roll when a Discipline ask for those values?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Situational, really<br /> Not many disciplines ask for those stats actually, and when it does, it is usually specified it works either vampire or human, but of course it is not only the case<br /> But I would say since Virtue is used in a character's sheet to show his spiritual and moral fiber \u2014 or lack thereof of a vampire/human? And Willpower is based on starting Courage, and Humanity (or its equivalent) is based on the total of starting Conscience and Self-Control (or some replacment)? That is a good guideline to figure out what to use.<br /> For example Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom use the Virtues of Orun (&quot;Heaven&quot;) and Aye (&quot;Earth&quot;), which represent the vampire's spirituality and humanity, respectively. Orun partially governs the vampire's Disciplines and to their ability to resist the workings of hostile magic, while Aye is used to resist frenzy and function during the day. Both of these traits also reflect the vampire's appearance: vampires with high Aye can pass for mortals, vampires with high Orun appear beatific, and vampires with low Orun appear bizarre or even monstrous.<br /> It is easy to decided how and what of those to use<br /> Kindred of the East's Yin, Yang, P'o, Hun and Demon Chi is a bit tricky but just follow the general guidline<br /> <br /> Then again, as I said when it comes to such specified stats, usually it is described it works on Vampire and/or Mortal<br /> But let's see an example!<br /> Dread gaze if I recall correctly uses Charisma + Intimidation difficulty equal to the victim\u2019s Wits + Courage<br /> If your vampire is fool enough to use it against a Garou in a crossower? Well the Garou don't have Courage stats, but have similar gifts, like True Fear that ask for a rolls Strength + Intimidation difficulty of the target's Willpower<br /> <br /> So as you can see, since in Vampire's system Willpower is based on starting Courage, and the gift/disicpline are similar, from that easy to deduct what to use. So just turn it around, a Garou's Courage is basically her Willpower<br /> \u200b<br /> But if you don't wantto complicate your life, just &quot;fake it till' make it&quot; and discuss with your storyteller<br /> Or if you are the storyteller, use your common sense and use what do you feel apropiate<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T11:56:18-07:00","id":1521047,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> thanks for the answers.<br /> <br /> I added a new question:<br /> <b>Which discipline better represents old civilization magic: Thaumaturgy, Koldonic Sorcery, or an assortment of Disciplines? </b><br /> <i>Essentially, what would old Egypt/Mesopotamia vampires have, I understand that Thaumaturgy is a recent invention, and that Koldunic Sorcery is Tzimisce but which one repressents the primal magic (Same way that Cruac does for Requiem).</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T12:34:18-07:00","id":1521052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520941-v20-various-doubts?p=1521047#post1521047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Which discipline better represents old civilization magic: Thaumaturgy, Koldonic Sorcery, or an assortment of Disciplines? </b><br /> <i>Essentially, what would old Egypt/Mesopotamia vampires have, I understand that Thaumaturgy is a recent invention, and that Koldunic Sorcery is Tzimisce but which one repressents the primal magic (Same way that Cruac does for Requiem).</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Egypt is one if not the oldest civilization, so the Settite Akhu is pretty &quot;old&quot;, not to mention it various rituals and practices heavly tied to the relegion<br /> Smiliarly, Dur-An-Ki; It is a very old form of magic, drawing from a huge variety of mortal religious traditions, and pre-dating Thaumaturgy, which it resembles in many ways.<br /> The Runes of the Einherjar likewise could be the base of (or an &quot;evolved form, but runes are basically the building blocks of any magical practices) an ancient form og magic, not that different from Ogham<br /> Nahuallotl is a form of religious blood magic practiced by the Tlacique and I think safe to say, everyone who is from Meso- and South-America<br /> But maybe the oldest of the oldest magic is the &quot;death magic&quot;, to contact the ancestors, aka. Necromancy and natue magic, shamanism, to honor and make deals with the spirits of nature and the world, ask them for help and power and respect them... in that case Koldunism<br /> I would say some shaman-vampire (or mortal for that matter) from 15-20.000 BC would be a Koldun/Necromancer","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 08-20-2023, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T13:34:14-07:00","id":1521060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520941-v20-various-doubts?p=1521052#post1521052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But maybe the oldest of the oldest magic is the &quot;death magic&quot;, to contact the ancestors, aka. Necromancy and natue magic, shamanism, to honor and make deals with the spirits of nature and the world, ask them for help and power and respect them... in that case Koldunism<br /> I would say some shaman-vampire (or mortal for that matter) from 15-20.000 BC would be a Koldun/Necromancer</div> </div> </div> </div>Either this or blood sorcery taught by an outside source, aka &quot;Dark&quot; Thaumaturgy. Despite the name it isn't really related to Tremere Thaumaturgy and invoking some entity for knowledge is as old as dirt- the &quot;Dark&quot; part is also somewhat of a point of view. Ancient Sumerian vampires petitioning their deities probably didn't really see it that way.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T00:51:55-07:00","id":1521104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520941-v20-various-doubts?p=1521047#post1521047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;23890&quot;]<b>Which discipline better represents old civilization magic: Thaumaturgy, Koldonic Sorcery, or an assortment of Disciplines? </b><br /> <i>Essentially, what would old Egypt/Mesopotamia vampires have, I understand that Thaumaturgy is a recent invention, and that Koldunic Sorcery is Tzimisce but which one repressents the primal magic (Same way that Cruac does for Requiem).</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Not all &quot;Thaumaturgy&quot; is a recent invention. Certainly the unique to Tremere Paths are recent in the sense they were developed in the past thousand years. But there has always been Thaumaturgy that pre-dated the Tremere and could be quite ancient. We should remember that Hermetic philosophy is supposed to be a rediscovery of magical knowledge that existed back in ancient Egyptian times.<br /> <br /> I would put all the Blood Magic Paths that are considered to be traditional vampire powers in that category. Weather Control and Movement of the Mind should be fairly old. I can easily see a vampire knowing Weather Control all the way back in Sumeria.<br /> <br /> Koldunic Sorcery should predate Tremere Hermeticism, but I do not believe it is incredibly ancient. It probably dates some time to the Iron Age. It might pre-date Tremere Paths by only 500 years or so. The most ancient Blood Magic paths should be dated to the Bronze Age and possibly even the Neolithic.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T02:45:02-07:00","id":1521110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520941-v20-various-doubts?p=1521104#post1521104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Koldunic Sorcery should predate Tremere Hermeticism, but I do not believe it is incredibly ancient. It probably dates some time to the Iron Age. It might pre-date Tremere Paths by only 500 years or so. The most ancient Blood Magic paths should be dated to the Bronze Age and possibly even the Neolithic.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure about that one<br /> I mean purely by sources, Yorak and Triglav, like several other Ancient Koldun were ebmraced <i>before</i> the Flood (and truth to be told even Baba Yaga probably was a proto-koldun)<br /> But more importantly, the deal the Eldest made with Kupala and the bloody war against the Shadow Lords also predate the Great Flood<br /> No matter the version you want to take, Koldunism is the Gift of Kupala or Kupala tainted and twisted the already existed Koldunism (Krainas in to Ways and Paths) Koldunism predate the Flood so I think if we take the ~10.000 years, Koldunism is from the Paleolithic Era<br /> (As a side note, People first migrated to Australia at least 65,000 years ago and both real world or WoD account the magic of the Aboriginal People of Australia is very similar to Koldunism; Aboriginal spirituality is defined as at the core of Aboriginal being, their very identity. It gives meaning to all aspects of life including relationships with one another and the environment. All objects are living and share the same soul and spirit as Aboriginals. There is a kinship with the environment. - tell me this is not &quot;Koldunism&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-08T16:49:36-07:00","id":1522284,"title":"","content":"Further questions, I dont want to open a new thread for them:<ul><li>Can Vicissitude heal or fix the Appearance of cainites with the <b>Mortuario </b>merit, or the <b>Harbingers of the Skulls</b>, <b>Samedi </b>bloodlines?</li> <li>The background<b> Memento de Morte </b>and the ritual<b> Death\u2019s Communion</b>, both add dice to the Necromancy rolls, is this for Paths, rituals or both?</li> <li>Same for <b>Mortuario </b>merit, it lowers difficulties of the Necromancy rolls, is this for Paths, rituals or both?</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 09-09-2023, 09:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T14:26:57-07:00","id":1522428,"title":"","content":"The Fiends can't undo clan deformities as it's beyond their power to do so as the curses were made by the oldest and most powerful vampire Caine and even the 3rd generation power can't match that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}